title: Remove deprecated sp_core hashing re-export
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    # Description

    Removes deprecated `sp_core` hashing re-exports as part of #11561.

    `sp-core` previously re-exported all of `sp-crypto-hashing` at the crate root (and as `sp_core::hashing`). Those re-exports were deprecated in 2024. This PR removes them and updates in-repo callers to use `sp_crypto_hashing` directly. `polkadot-sdk-frame::hashing` now re-exports from `sp_crypto_hashing` instead of via `sp_core`.

    Does not close #11561.

    ## Integration

    Downstream code must stop importing hashing helpers from `sp_core`:

    ```diff
    - use sp_core::{H256, keccak_256};
    + use sp_core::H256;
    + use sp_crypto_hashing::keccak_256;

    - sp_core::blake2_256(data)
    + sp_crypto_hashing::blake2_256(data)

    - sp_core::hashing::twox_128(b"System")
    + sp_crypto_hashing::twox_128(b"System")
    ```
    `polkadot_sdk_frame::hashing::*` remains available `(now backed by sp_crypto_hashing)`.

    Review Notes

    - Removes pub use sp_crypto_hashing::{self as hashing, *} from substrate/primitives/core/src/lib.rs
    - Updates polkadot-sdk-frame hashing module to pub use sp_crypto_hashing::*
    - Mechanical caller updates across revive, election-provider-multi-phase, snowbridge, migrations, people, staking-async, benchmarking-cli, network-statement, xcm-simulator example, zombienet-sdk tests
crates:
- name: snowbridge-inbound-queue-primitives
  bump: major
- name: snowbridge-test-utils
  bump: major
- name: xcm-simulator-example
  bump: major
